---
// The peer evaluation generator (#438). The component reads the roster in
// the browser only, so it mounts client-side and nothing reads files at
// build time.
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";
import PeerEvaluationGenerator from "../../components/tools/PeerEvaluationGenerator.svelte";
---

<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    description:
      "Generate the peer evaluation survey and its contact list from the Canvas roster.",
    editUrl: false,
    head: [{ attrs: { content: "noindex", name: "robots" }, tag: "meta" }],
    pagefind: false,
    title: "Peer Evaluation Survey",
  }}
>
  <p>
    Drop the Canvas roster with groups to get the Qualtrics survey and the
    contact list. The file is read in your browser and never uploaded.
  </p>

  <PeerEvaluationGenerator client:only="svelte" />

  <h2>Where the inputs come from and what to do next</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      In Canvas, People, Groups: export the group set's roster with groups as
      CSV (<code>name, canvas_user_id, user_id, login_id, sections,
      group_name, canvas_group_id, group_id</code>).
    </li>
    <li>
      Drop it above, pick the survey and the course and term, and download
      both files. Students alone on a team or in no team are listed above and
      left out; a team over 10 stops the run.
    </li>
    <li>
      In Qualtrics, Create a new project, Survey, From a file: import the
      <code>.qsf</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      In the directory, create a mailing list from the contact-list CSV. Every
      column maps by its header: <code>Email</code>, <code>Team</code>,
      <code>TeamSize</code>, <code>SelfFloor</code>, and
      <code>Team Member 1</code> to <code>9</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Set the availability dates on the distribution, not in the survey.
    </li>
    <li>
      Distribute by email with personal links only. The survey is by invitation,
      so the anonymous link does not open it.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    If the Loop &amp; Merge version fails to import or the staff test shows a
    wrong page, regenerate with "One block per teammate slot": same
    questions, one block per slot behind a branch.
  </p>
</StarlightPage>
